                            {
                                "target_word": "scald",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5128c98e-05a6-3875-b465-aa9153d33f93",
                                        "entry_id": "0982c3f1-7a8b-37f9-ad1c-7f6611656e27",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Scaliness; a scabby skin disease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b92797f3-50c3-4f01-b158-3aad861ddc7b",
                                                "sense_id": "5128c98e-05a6-3875-b465-aa9153d33f93",
                                                "text": "Her craftie head was altogether bald, / And as in hate of honorable eld, / Was ouergrowne with scurfe and filthy scald[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e4c5f83-6f96-4a36-96f4-a928f2900fd2",
                                                "sense_id": "5128c98e-05a6-3875-b465-aa9153d33f93",
                                                "text": "Some heale Horses, some cure men, some the plague, some the scald [translating teigne], some the cough, some one kinde of scab, and some another[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scald",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17bad357-7dd6-3f9e-b9bf-4f4179b9d6e2",
                                        "entry_id": "8e9b8351-5a1d-3eef-b445-ce9fa558eeb4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affected with the scab; scabby."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6559bddb-d64d-4811-86a4-12e0d03a8fe0",
                                                "sense_id": "17bad357-7dd6-3f9e-b9bf-4f4179b9d6e2",
                                                "text": "and let us knog our / prains together to be revenge on this same scald, scurvy, / cogging companion,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "947f299f-c7dd-3b0e-af25-7950c290cd5c",
                                        "entry_id": "8e9b8351-5a1d-3eef-b445-ce9fa558eeb4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Paltry; worthless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "694803b8-ea3e-4a42-831f-d67e79a603f7",
                                                "sense_id": "947f299f-c7dd-3b0e-af25-7950c290cd5c",
                                                "text": "Would it not grieue a King to be so abuſ’d?\nAnd haue a thouſand horſmen tane away?\nAnd which is worſe to haue his Diadem\nSought for by ſuch ſcalde knaues as loue him not?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e8cf457-f5d1-462a-a5c3-9c9e095a9dc4",
                                                "sense_id": "947f299f-c7dd-3b0e-af25-7950c290cd5c",
                                                "text": "Saucy lictors / Will catch at us like strumpets, and scald rhymers / Ballad us out o' tune."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scald",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5ce4ccb-59b3-3b14-b603-b1d3cad46043",
                                        "entry_id": "2350efea-89af-3704-a278-66614bb2fd68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of skald."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05437db8-9d54-452e-b511-db89023cfbb8",
                                                "sense_id": "f5ce4ccb-59b3-3b14-b603-b1d3cad46043",
                                                "text": "The fire was spreading rapidly through all parts of the castle, when Ulrica, who had first kindled it, appeared on a turret, in the guise of one of the ancient furies, yelling forth a war-song, such as was of yore chaunted on the field of battle by the scalds of the yet heathen Saxons."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b694bba8-8096-4dcf-b2f8-fef81151bb63",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5914608-2cff-3f83-a6f7-fb68f33f955a",
